 "client_feedback": [
  {
   "date": "2026-10-26",
   "from": "Mark (EMBLEM-NLP), looking at design 2 on an iPhone",
   "said": "Not a fan of this composed hero image and the copy remains exactly the same as our first version which is an issue",
   "changes": [
    "The home hero is now a real photograph, not a composed image (a hand holding a phone; cropped, colour-matched and with a small printed maker's name retouched out) with the carrier logos on a white bar over its lower edge. The link preview image is a plain crop of the same photograph. No page may carry a composed image: imagery.max_composites_per_page is 0 and imagery.hero_not_composite is on.",
    "Design 2 has its own wording (designs/design-2/content.json and its own pages). distinctness.copy compares it with design 1 and fails a build that reuses design 1's page titles, descriptions, headings, sentences or phrases. Since the independent read of v4 and v5 found light rewrites that a strict match cannot see, a sentence counts as reused when it is 60% similar to one of design 1's (sentence_similarity 0.6, down from 0.85). The old build (v3) fails every one of those checks; the new one passes.",
    "New accuracy question: copy_written_for_this_design."
   ]
  }
 ]
